WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:07.180
There is a stunning and hilarious and pathetic
and disturbing new report from The New York

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:14.780
Times about Donald Trump threatening Mike
Pence with designating him as a pussy.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:21.949
And that is a quote that is that his presidential
speech here, Mike Pence and Donald Trump had

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:28.250
a falling out, unlike any that I recall seeing
between a president and Vice President Donald

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.250
Trump.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.450
We knew in the days leading up to the January
6th, counting of the electoral votes and what

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:37.860
became a riotous insurrection in Washington,
D.C., had been pressuring Mike Pence to do

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:42.920
it, do it, take steal the election, figure
out a way to do the right thing.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:48.970
And we have actually now learned that Donald
Trump specifically said to Mike Pence in the

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:58.980
lead up to that day early last week, quote,
You can either go down in history as a patriot.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:06.010
Wait for it or you can go down in history
as a pussy, of course, Mike Pence, Mike Pence

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:12.740
is a dangerous ideologue, extremist, but he
realized I can't steal the election there.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.100
I don't have the power to steal the election.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.470
Even if I wanted to steal the election, I
couldn't do it.

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:23.120
And very quickly, as it became clear Mike
Pence was not going to stand in the way and

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.970
as the riotous insurrection grew on Wednesday
afternoon, Donald Trump took to Twitter before

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:31.530
Twitter banned him and said Mike Pence couldn't
do it.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.060
Mike Pence couldn't do it.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:38.000
They then went up until Monday without even
speaking, despite the fact that Mike Pence

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.030
was put in physical danger at the Capitol
by the riotous insurrection that Donald Trump

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.030
incited.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:53.030
And they reportedly had what is being sort
of, I don't even know, vaguely described as

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:56.150
a productive meeting on Monday.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.189
Unclear what the relationship is between the
two of them.

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:03.170
So there's a few different things going on
here.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:10.440
One of the things we have to be really careful
about and we talk about reputation is framing

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:18.910
normal behavior as heroic or virtuous, because
in comparison, so many people have been behaving

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.680
like absolute lunatics.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.540
And what I mean by that is Lindsey Graham
is an example.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.700
We talked about this earlier in the week.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:32.100
Lindsey Graham on very late Wednesday, early
Thursday morning, last week, spoke during

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.090
the counting of the electoral vote.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:37.000
And he said things that are just the way it
is.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.800
Lindsey Graham said, our duty is just to count
the votes.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:47.040
Some of these objections are out of scope
for the House and Senate in a joint session

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.370
to really even deal with things, went to courts
and courts, made decisions.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:55.050
And he was held up as a hero for like six
hours.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:58.569
Until then, he said insane things the next
morning and then also the following night

00:02:58.569 --> 00:02:59.980
on Fox News.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:05.470
And one of the problems is that we talk about
the Overton Window and the value of pulling

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:11.030
the Overton Window to the left, for example,
to bring the center to the left to mainstream

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:12.680
progressive ideas.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:17.110
But there's another Overton Window that's
been absolutely brutalized during the last

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:23.130
four years, and it relates to hyper normalization
when you have a two month campaign from veritable

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:30.220
lunatics like Donald Trump and Rudy Giuliani
and Sidney Powell and Josh Holly and Lin Wood

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.910
and you know, the full list of these people
to insist without evidence the election was

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:35.130
stolen, stolen this that.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:39.569
The other thing when somebody simply says.

00:03:39.569 --> 00:03:44.269
This goes beyond the limits of what we are
allowed to do based on our appointments here

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:50.200
in the House and Senate, they seem so reasonable
and people start saying these are the good

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.200
Republicans.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:56.959
No, Lindsey was on TV the next night begging
for mercy for Trump and saying impeachment

00:03:56.959 --> 00:03:57.959
would be divisive.

00:03:57.959 --> 00:04:01.060
Well, then he should have thought of that
when he did something worthy of impeachment.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:04.430
That would have been the time to think about
it before it became too late.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:09.560
So let's we're ending Donald Trump's term
with something very similar to what I said

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:14.540
at the beginning of Donald Trump's term, which
is we must work hard.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:21.380
And it's really tough to avoid the hyper normalization
when so much of what we see daily is outrageous,

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:26.110
when what we see every week would have been
a one year scandal for Barack Obama had it

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:34.230
happened, then it's very difficult not to
see been this slightly less cartoonish, but

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:39.449
still not benign right wing radicals as being
sort of sensible.

00:04:39.449 --> 00:04:46.229
And, you know, when we say Mitt Romney actually
seems to be making some sense, we're not saying

00:04:46.229 --> 00:04:47.479
we agree with him politically.

00:04:47.479 --> 00:04:51.500
At least I'm not we're not saying he's a friend
of progressives.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:57.229
We're simply saying he has been consistent
on what are the limits of the House and Senate

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:59.050
and presidential power, et cetera.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.110
I still disagree with him on tax policy.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.460
I still disagree with him on a whole bunch
of other things.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.490
But at least he's been consistent.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:12.390
Lindsey Graham is not that Mike Pence is not
that Mike Pence was limited not by his delusions

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.390
of grandeur.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:14.979
We don't know what he might have wanted to
do.

00:05:14.979 --> 00:05:16.570
Could he have gotten away with it?

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:21.300
He was limited by the fact that he can't actually
do the thing Donald Trump was asking him to

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.300
do.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:26.370
And it's a very important thing to remember
as we get past this administration and it

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:30.750
gets into the rearview mirror and we think
about it, we want to remember it for what

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:31.750
it was.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.370
It was hard to fight the normalization while
it was going on.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:38.370
And we have to remember that we're going to
have to work just as hard to fight it in retrospect

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:41.120
and really remember just how insane it was.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:44.050
We will ultimately see what happens with impeachment
in the Senate.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:51.490
But the it it is at the same time extraordinary
that a president denounced his own vice president.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:55.880
But Mike Pence deserves no praise for not
doing the thing Trump asked them to do because

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.460
in the end, he couldn't do it.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.820
It simply is not something that he could do.

